From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] settings: AD5X bed heat soak; checks after a nozzle change

Settings > Printer gets a "Bed Heat Soak" row after Nozzle Size, shown
only where Klipper has the ad5x_soak object, with "On · 60 °C 7:00" or
"Off" as its second line. Its overlay has the on/off switch
(BED_SOAK_ENABLE), the calibrated times per bed temperature and a
calibration: a bed temperature (60-110 °C) and Calibrate, refused during
a print or above 40 °C on the bed, confirmed first. BED_SOAK_CALIBRATE
holds the G-code queue for 20-35 minutes and answers when it ends, so it
goes out with a 75 minute timeout and the screen follows the object's
`running` meanwhile (and alone, should the answer never come): Klipper's
status line, the rounds so far and Stop, which is the Klipper API
endpoint printer.ad5x_soak.abort (no G-code reaches Klipper while it
runs). The end shows Klipper's result line or its error, also as a toast
when the overlay is closed. The object joins the status subscription.

After Settings > Nozzle Size changed the size and Klipper is back with
it, a dialog offers the hotend PID tune and the Z offset test (Run /
Later). Run starts a targeted setup session over PID, Z offset and the
save step, whose PID step is sent with heaters=extruder: targeted
sessions now carry per-step start parameters, cleared when the session
ends and never read by the first-start wizard. "Run Setup Wizard" passes
none, so it still tunes nozzle and bed. The wizard's own Nozzle Size step
offers nothing (the tuning steps follow it anyway).

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
